  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STFA Joint Programme for the Northern Region of Afghanistan: Addressing Basic Human Needs through the ABADEI Strategy - Outcome 4 Community Planning and Social Cohesion</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PUNOs will support communities to access justice through mediation and alternative dispute resolution mechanisms. Positive customary and traditional practices for conflict resolutions will be strengthened combined with provision of counselling and legal aid services. PUNOs will also promote community dialogue and engagement to prevent conflict and violent extremism (PVE), strengthen social cohesion and facilitate reconciliation. Broad dialogue platforms and early warning mechanisms will be enhanced with participation of women, youth, community leaders such as religious, traditional and tribal elders, IDPs, returnees and minority groups. PUNOs will leverage on existing peacebuilding structures including through Community Development Councils (CDC) and peace committees or, where appropriate, will create new mechanisms to enable a conducive peacebuilding environment. Capacities of civil society organizations (CSOs), community-based organizations (CBOs) and women and youth groups will also be strengthened as key players for local peacebuilding.</narrative>
  </description>
